            <ArticleTitle>Constrained total hip arthroplasty in a paediatric patient with cerebral palsy and painful dislocation of the hip. A case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>655-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a patient with cerebral palsy, of normal intelligence, who could not walk but who by the age of 16 had been successfully managed with a staged bilateral total hip arthroplasty using a constrained liner.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
